      "baseline_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is Sophia Taylor with user ID sophia_taylor_9065. Her reservation number is PEP4E0. She says she added insurance but it's not showing up online. She's flying with family who have insurance, and she wants it added persistently. She doesn't want to be transferred.\n\nFirst, I need to check the reservation details to see if insurance is actually there. The function get_reservation_details can help. Let me call that with reservation_id PEP4E0. Once I get the details, I can check the insurance status. If it's not there, maybe there was an error in adding it. Then, I need to figure out how to add insurance. Wait, according to the policy, travel insurance can only be added at the time of booking. If the reservation was already made without insurance, can it be added later? The policy says the agent should ask about insurance during booking, and once booked, it can't be added. So if the user didn't include it initially, maybe it's not possible. But the user insists she added it. Maybe there's a system error. Alternatively, maybe she tried to add it through another method. \n\nBut according to the tools, there's no function to add insurance after booking. The book_reservation function includes insurance as a parameter, but modifying it later isn't covered. The update functions (update_reservation_flights, etc.) don't mention insurance. So if insurance wasn't added during booking, the user can't add it later. So the agent needs to check the reservation details and inform the user. If insurance isn't there, explain that it can't be added now and suggest rebooking if possible. But the user insists persistently. However, the policy says not to transfer unless necessary. Since the user doesn't want to be transferred, I have to handle it. But if the tools don't allow adding insurance post-booking, I have to inform her that it's not possible. So first step is to get the reservation details to confirm the current status.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_reservation_details\", \"arguments\": {\"reservation_id\": \"PEP4E0\"}}\n",
